{"id":"gap-co-canal","title":"Great Allegheny Passage and C&O Canal","who":"Classic route · Pittsburgh to Washington DC traffic-free","when":"April to October","vehicle":"Hybrid, gravel or touring bike, 5–7 days","kind":"bike","color":"#334155","summary":"About 335 miles without cars: the Great Allegheny Passage rail trail over the Eastern Continental Divide to Cumberland, then the old C&O canal towpath down the Potomac past lock houses, Paw Paw tunnel and Harpers Ferry to Georgetown. Smooth on the GAP, rougher and muddier on the towpath.","sources":[{"label":"Softwhere: GAP and C&O trip logistics and gear (October 2025)","url":"https://blog.softwhere.org/2025/10/05/gap-co-trip-logistics-gear"},{"label":"NPS: bike the C&O Canal towpath","url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/bike-the-c-o-canal-towpath.htm"}],"approximate":"Main towns; the line follows the trails.","km":530,"bbox":[-80.0098,38.9052,-77.0628,40.4415],"stops":[{"name":"Pittsburgh","place":"Point State Park, Pittsburgh","at":[40.4415,-80.0101],"text":"Mile 0 at the fountain where three rivers meet."},{"name":"Ohiopyle","place":"Ohiopyle, Pennsylvania","at":[39.8699,-79.4929],"text":"Waterfalls and rafting on the Youghiogheny.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Jonathan%27s_Run_Falls.jpg/500px-Jonathan%27s_Run_Falls.jpg","page":"Ohiopyle State Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jonathan%27s_Run_Falls.jpg","credit":"Hubert Stoffels from Pittsburgh, USA","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Meyersdale","place":"Meyersdale, Pennsylvania","at":[39.8137,-79.0247],"text":"The Salisbury viaduct, then the Eastern Continental Divide.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Straighten_into_Salisbury_Viaduct_%28cut%29.jpg/500px-Straighten_into_Salisbury_Viaduct_%28cut%29.jpg","page":"Salisbury Viaduct","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Straighten_into_Salisbury_Viaduct_%28cut%29.jpg","credit":"daveynin from United States","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Cumberland","place":"Cumberland, Maryland","at":[39.6526,-78.7624],"text":"The GAP ends; mile 184 of the C&O towpath starts.","source":{"label":"Softwhere (2025)","url":"https://blog.softwhere.org/2025/10/05/gap-co-trip-logistics-gear"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Cumberland_Aerial_2022.jpg/500px-Cumberland_Aerial_2022.jpg","page":"Cumberland, Maryland","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cumberland_Aerial_2022.jpg","credit":"Matthew Binebrink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Paw Paw Tunnel","place":"Paw Paw Tunnel","at":[39.5503,-78.4597],"text":"A 3,118 ft canal tunnel: walk your bike with a light.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/C%26O_Canal_NHP_Paw_Paw_Tunnel_Hill_Trail_Ribbon_Cutting_%286286314760%29.jpg/500px-C%26O_Canal_NHP_Paw_Paw_Tunnel_Hill_Trail_Ribbon_Cutting_%286286314760%29.jpg","page":"Paw Paw Tunnel","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C%26O_Canal_NHP_Paw_Paw_Tunnel_Hill_Trail_Ribbon_Cutting_%286286314760%29.jpg","credit":"C&amp;O Canal NHP","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Hancock","place":"Hancock, Maryland","at":[39.6994,-78.1821],"text":"A paved rail trail runs alongside here.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Hancock_main_street.jpg/500px-Hancock_main_street.jpg","page":"Hancock, Maryland","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hancock_main_street.jpg","credit":"Aude","license":"CC BY-SA 2.5"}},{"name":"Harpers Ferry","place":"Harpers Ferry, West Virginia","at":[39.3234,-77.732],"text":"Where the Shenandoah meets the Potomac."},{"name":"Great Falls","place":"Great Falls, Maryland","at":[38.9977,-77.2529],"text":"The Potomac's wildest rapids.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Great_Falls_Potomac_River_VA.JPG/500px-Great_Falls_Potomac_River_VA.JPG","page":"Great Falls (Potomac River)","sour